APPU GOUNDAN: Yeah.

00:25:32.675 --> 00:25:35.776
AUDIENCE: How do you integrate
it to the Maven release cycle?

00:25:35.776 --> 00:25:37.650
QINGYANG CHEN: So the
question is, how do you

00:25:37.650 --> 00:25:39.520
integrate it to the Maven--

00:25:39.520 --> 00:25:42.317
the Raven cycle of
the life cycle, right?

00:25:42.317 --> 00:25:42.900
AUDIENCE: Yes.

00:25:42.900 --> 00:25:43.733
QINGYANG CHEN: Yeah.

00:25:43.733 --> 00:25:48.300
So you can actually add it
to a phase-- lifecycle phase

00:25:48.300 --> 00:25:49.760
and just have it execute.

00:25:49.760 --> 00:25:55.050
So the plugin-- you can define
executions for the build goal

00:25:55.050 --> 00:25:59.400
and have it execute on the phase
that you want it to execute on.

00:25:59.400 --> 00:26:02.100
APPU GOUNDAN: As long as
it happens after compile.

00:26:02.100 --> 00:26:04.110
Presumably, you would
put it in package,

00:26:04.110 --> 00:26:06.670
which is where most
builders or packagers go,

00:26:06.670 --> 00:26:10.010
and we're kind of
a packaging tool.

00:26:10.010 --> 00:26:13.080
QINGYANG CHEN: Yeah,
and this is also

00:26:13.080 --> 00:26:15.613
available as a Gradle
plugin, so in Gradle, it

00:26:15.613 --> 00:26:19.320
would be you can set a
dependency for the Jib task

00:26:19.320 --> 00:26:21.990
on whichever other tasks
you want to run it after.

00:26:25.520 --> 00:26:26.429
Yes.

00:26:26.429 --> 00:26:28.345
AUDIENCE: What about
