00:26:35.960 --> 00:26:38.750
that's burned into the
image, but if you're running

00:26:38.750 --> 00:26:40.460
the image on, say,
Kubernetes, you

00:26:40.460 --> 00:26:43.873
can define the volume
amounts for the container.

00:26:43.873 --> 00:26:44.373
Yeah.

00:26:51.618 --> 00:26:52.584
Yes.

00:26:52.584 --> 00:26:55.240
AUDIENCE: Is it
configurable if I do not

00:26:55.240 --> 00:26:57.069
