00:27:20.490 --> 00:27:21.766
that you want to add, right?

00:27:21.766 --> 00:27:23.221
AUDIENCE: JFrog [INAUDIBLE].

00:27:23.221 --> 00:27:24.096
QINGYANG CHEN: Sorry?

00:27:24.096 --> 00:27:25.500
AUDIENCE: JFrog registry.

00:27:25.500 --> 00:27:26.710
APPU GOUNDAN: Oh, their
container registry.

00:27:26.710 --> 00:27:27.990
QINGYANG CHEN: Oh,
container registry.

00:27:27.990 --> 00:27:29.614
So the container
registries-- it should

00:27:29.614 --> 00:27:33.990
support most cloud providers
for container registries.

00:27:33.990 --> 00:27:37.080
You can also even use
a private registry

00:27:37.080 --> 00:27:41.040
that you set up
yourself, so you can--

00:27:41.040 --> 00:27:43.260
for example, you can even
push it to a local registry

00:27:43.260 --> 00:27:43.760
if you want.

00:27:43.760 --> 00:27:45.610
So you can run a local registry.

00:27:45.610 --> 00:27:49.410
You can just have it be
local host, whatever port,

00:27:49.410 --> 00:27:50.552
slash whatever image.

00:27:50.552 --> 00:27:52.260
So the first part of
that image reference

00:27:52.260 --> 00:27:55.240
is going to be the registry
that you want to push it to.

00:27:55.240 --> 00:28:00.670
So whichever other Container
Registry that you want to use--

00:28:00.670 --> 00:28:01.930
it should be able to do it.

00:28:01.930 --> 00:28:04.870
If it doesn't, let us know.

00:28:04.870 --> 00:28:06.100
